{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"32a83272-5541-46ce-8934-1efeb9c053a8","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented the fix for the HR range generator:\n\n- Added a constant **`LTHR = 172`** to provide the known lactate threshold heart rate.\n- Updated **`hr_target`** to optionally compute absolute BPM values when `LTHR` is supplied, otherwise retain the original percentage‑of‑LTHR behavior.\n- Modified **`build_step`** to pass `LTHR` to `hr_target`, ensuring all steps generate BPM ranges.\n\nThe generator now outputs HR values directly in BPM (e.g., Warm‑up 117‑129 bpm, Tempo 151‑160 bpm, Float 129‑141 bpm, Cool‑down 112‑124 bpm), matching the planned zones instead of being clamped to the watch's internal zones.\n\nDetails of the changes and the rationale are documented in the generated **[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/32a83272-5541-46ce-8934-1efeb9c053a8/ANSWER.md)**.\n","duration_seconds":61.947637,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":30375,"output_tokens":4481,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":243904,"total_tokens":34856}}}
